  "artifacts": {
    "abstract": {
      "page": 1,
      "text": "We argue that BPS ansatzes, entering manifestly vacuum BPS monopole solutions to equations of motion in the (Minkowskian) non-Abelian Higgs model play the role of some electric form-factors and that this implies (soft) violating the CP-invariance of the mentioned model, similar to taking place in the Euclidian Yang-Mills (YM) theory with instantons, generating the θ-term in the appropriate effective Hamiltonian. PACS: 14.80.Bn, 14.80.Hv."
    },
